A||||3||theogre||CarParts vs Wreanchead||||1||
Z||000000||theogre||03-03-2000||08:14 PM||||Well....<P>I've ordered from both now. Was an interesting adventure.<P>For a start, more parts books than I can count insist 87 4 cyl still has a distributor, and a Thermac. This was a problem with CarParts.com as well. Wrenchead got it right.<P>Over all I found Wrenchead easier to find things. ((Altho this AC-Delco + battery cable looks awfully short....)) They list everything the 87 4 cyl uses correctly. ((I'll have to check out that + cable....))<P>Unless you are pretty sure what you want I found CarParts listings hard to decifer at times.<P>On CarPart good side tho is the online help. Once first level help confirmed that the 87 listing was wrong I was forwarded to someone who could lookup the proper part. (Accel 140017 coils)<P>Once he found the part and price he put in an order and a CarParts rep called my home to confirm the order and complete the credit card transaction, at 9:30PM EST. (BTW. The Accel DIS coils are actually less expencive at CarParts than the OEM coils are there or anywhere else. Shipping was about $5. [Pep Boys wanted $35+ each for the OEM ones.])<P>On the negative side, niether one offers a simple inventory search. You are stuck with only what is listed online or calling. And a good chunk of things are not online at either site becuase they are expanding them so fast. ||||reg||1
Z||000001||DXR_DAD||03-03-2000||08:55 PM||||Ogre, after reading many of your post on the DIS and the problem with sensors I have replaced all of them on my 87, all from wrenchead, their prices were alot cheaper than the local parts house. No problems with them so far.<P>Thanks for the info its good to know these things.||||reg||1
Z||000002||batboy||03-03-2000||09:47 PM||||I haven't ordered from wrenchhead yet, but I will eventually. I have used their site several times to see what brand parts are available and to look up part numbers. It also gives you a rough idea of price in the local parts stores.||||reg||1
Z||000003||87ECO5||03-03-2000||11:33 PM||||Thanks for the eval, Ogre.  We REALLY appreciate it!||||reg||1
